Z||000000||Wade87GT||10-16-2000||12:26 PM||||I just received the latest flyer from the Fiero Store. They have a new front brake upgrade kit using 9.8" vented rotors, pads, hubs, and larger piston bore calipers. It also comes with caliper mount brackets that look very much like the existing Fiero ones, instead of adding on mount adapters. It's also a true "bolt-on" kit. For me, time = money, so this could be a better option instead of going with the Baretta upgrade (which requires machining down the rotors, turning them into hubs). I'm still running a stock motor so I don't need massive 12" braking power yet. In comparing, does anybody know the diameter of the Baretta rotors?||||reg||1
Z||000001||elfiero||10-16-2000||02:27 PM||||they are about the same as stock,9.somthin.||||reg||6
