Z||000012||Zorba||10-18-2000||01:51 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by the need for speed:<BR><B>is ryane still selling fiero stuff </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>What I don't like is to pay for stuff and wait 2 months or so to get it. I know someone in CA who used ZR-1 Corvette brakes all around on his 383 strokers v8 plus the defunct rear bump steer kit.<BR>You only need better brakes if you have more engine power.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000013||bHooper||10-18-2000||07:33 AM||||Zorba, I disagree about only needing better brakes if you have more power. <P>I have a factory Gt and I would love to be able to stop on a dime!  Even though I dont have a gagillian horsepower, I still tend to drive above the limts, or to the edge daily.  Therefore, I require a better set of brakes, and suspension.<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000014||Wade87GT||10-18-2000||10:17 AM||||I'm with Hoop on braking needs. So far I've been able to maneuver through impending disasters on the road using a combination of steering, brakes and the gas pedal. But I can't lock up the brakes now (225/50/16 all around with Carbomet pads), so that tells me my system is inadequate. Your best braking occurs at the limits of tire adhesion, just prior to lock-up. That's what ABS does for you. Unfortunately, I can't find anybody locally to machine my rotors into hubs (or get it right the first time) so I'm going with the F/S kit. Anything is better than what I've got now.||||reg||1
Z||000015||william_thorniii||10-18-2000||11:09 AM||||nfs,<P>To answer your qestion (afterall you must be curious to ask twice... and no one must know to ignore you twice), yes Ryane is officially out of the Fiero suspension/brake business.  They have said that they will continue to sell limited amounts of Fiero parts until they run out of supply.  It was a great loss, but a good business decision for them.  There is so much more money in the import market.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||13
Z||000016||Standard||10-19-2000||02:25 AM||||I have the stock brakes, and I can lock up the front no problem.. even got a big cloud of smoke when I wasn't paying attention one day on the freeway  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>The Fiero brake system in good condition will stop better than lots of cars.  The problem is that it won't stop quickly many times in a row, because of the solid rotors.  That's why the GA upgrade is so popular..<P>As for me, I'm saving up for the Ultimate Garage Big Brake conversion..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.ultimategarage.com/fiero3.jpg">  <A HREF="http://www.ultimategarage.com/bbfiero.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.ultimategarage.com/bbfiero.html</A> <P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 151,000 miles and counting!         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">      <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/asthanos.gif"> ||||reg||1
